  "_build_note": "IRPT_DASHBD cell DB-b-7 (workstream B): the reporting gold account_return_daily on its own clock. handler.py resolves T-1 with lib/trading_calendar.py, takes the gold's newest landed date= partition, and runs the producer's own functions for every trading day after it through T-1 (at most 10 per fire), for the accounts of that newest partition; it does not call the producer's dim_return_method write. pandas/pyarrow from the existing irpt-performance-native-layer (read-only data source, no new layer version published). Planned, not applied: the apply is the issuer's act. The map key is the SCOPE-LESS builder name of the artifact (name('irpt', None, 'reporting-gold', 'lambda')): the commit-time naming gate refuses a NEW hand-kept firm token in a JSON key or value, so the artifact carries no firm token while the function it deploys (builder name with the firm's short form, from the Terraform root) and its execution role are firm-scoped builder output in infra/aws/terraform/investor-reporting/reporting-gold/.",
